   "title": "Unit Economics (price → margin)",
   "purpose": "CC's true-total-cost stack (lecture slide, Step 3): profit = price − (unit cost + first/last-mile logistics + warehousing + payout/platform fees + refunds + creator commission/ads). Payout fee = price × % + fixed per order (CC: 6% + $0.30, which is 7.00% of a $29.99 price — the slide's 'platform fixed fee' line). Fixed-cost share = landed share + fee share; gross margin (max commission) = 1 − fixed share − refund reserve; company margin = gross margin − creator+ads allocation (CC: 30%). The sample row reproduces CC's worked example: 31.92% → 38.92% → 56.08% → 26.08% → 54.76 in home currency (FX 7). Classification follows CC's value-gap triage; the 60% profit-product cut-off is an aiOS default (CC only gives ≈50–60% = traffic product).",
